Mining accident

An explosion in the Caroline mine (Blackstone, New Hampshire) cost the lives of three miners. Witnesses claim tremors were felt up to half a mile from the mine and the bang could be heard from inside homes even with the windows closed.

The cause of the explosion, and whether it could be avoided, is yet to be determined. Our reporter has not been able to contact either of the mine's co-owners: George Whitehead was unavailable, while Jacob Hyde refused to comment on the accident.
We will provide our readers with further details as the story unfolds.
/*TB*/

