Father, 

The news of your grave illness has broken my heart. Mother informs me that your condition is serious, but I do hope this letter reaches you in time.

As you know, I moved to the Old Continent three years ago. I traveled for a while before finally settling down in London. I am sure you will be pleased to know I have realized one of your biggest dreams for me and become a doctor. I do believe I could not have become the respectable and esteemed man I am today if it was not for your strict upbringing and the moral fiber you planted in me.

I had no idea your illness would grow so severe that we might not have another chance to speak face-to-face. There is so much I wanted to tell you! I dare say I have managed to fathom the very nature of evil that has consumed the human soul since the beginning of time. I used to think we are born that way, but I was wrong. In fact, evil gradually seeps into us as we mature and develop. In Europe – especially in France – it is believed that sickness is caused by tiny organisms called bacteria. I have come to believe that this is similar to how all corruption spreads. We do not become beasts at random – we are infected by our so-called neighbors.

Here in London, the main cause of depravity are those vile women that citizens call prostitutes, although to me they are ordinary whores. They are the ones who spread all evil, consuming souls and minds.

At night, after work, I set out on the streets of London and seek out the worst, most abominable whores. Then, in the darkness of alleys, I plunge my unfailing scalpel into their viscera, whispering my prayers. At times I can see that thing leaving their bodies – sometimes it looks like a slimy viper writhing under the skin, other times it looks more like black worms – I have no doubt this is how grave sin is materialized.

I must say that my actions have brought me some notoriety, so now you can be proud of your son – the son who silently takes away the sins of the world by night. Isn’t it amusing that the London press has dubbed me Jack the Ripper?

Your faithful son,

Edward
